
==========================================================================
  QIF-AS-CNOT VERIFICATION
==========================================================================

  Term: let (f, x') = (qif x then X else I) in f x'
  Elaborated: make_branch + case_hom (see qif_apply above)
  Claim: this term is exactly CNOT with x as control, x' as target.

==========================================================================
  CHECK 1: verify_ctrl_unitary against mathematical ctrl^1(X)
==========================================================================
  PASS  qif_apply == ctrl^1(X)  fidelity=1.0000000000

==========================================================================
  CHECK 2: eq_circ against independent `ctrl gate_x` construction
==========================================================================
  PASS  qif_apply == ctrl q gate_x  fidelity=1.0000000000

==========================================================================
  TRUTH TABLE (derived from term semantics)
==========================================================================

  Notation: |x⟩ ⊗ |x'⟩ = |x, x'⟩   (x is the Bool tag; x' is Q)

  |0, 0⟩ → case picks I  → I|0⟩ = |0⟩ → |0, 0⟩
  |0, 1⟩ → case picks I  → I|1⟩ = |1⟩ → |0, 1⟩
  |1, 0⟩ → case picks X  → X|0⟩ = |1⟩ → |1, 1⟩
  |1, 1⟩ → case picks X  → X|1⟩ = |0⟩ → |1, 0⟩

  That is the CNOT truth table with x = control, x' = target.
  Check 1 above verified this via full 4x4 unitary equality
  against the mathematically-constructed ctrl^1(X) matrix,
  which covers every basis state (and every superposition).

